  "necessity_paragraph": "The patient presents with recurrent episodes of palpitations and lightheadedness, raising concern for paroxysmal atrial fibrillation in the context of a personal history of transient ischemic attacks and cerebral infarction. To evaluate for potential arrhythmic causes of these transient cerebral ischemic events and guide anticoagulation management, a cardiac event monitoring study (CPT 93271) is ordered. This monitoring is clinically necessary to identify the arrhythmic etiology of the patient's symptoms and to inform the management of their history of cerebral infarction (I48.0)."
